      "text": "A bar chart compares two test averages, 92 and 96 marks. Its vertical axis starts at 90, so the second bar appears three times as tall as the first. Choose the correct criticism: 1 = the second average is truly three times the first; 2 = the truncated axis exaggerates the difference; 3 = bars may never show averages."
    }
  ],
